{
  "Lets users select files with a button or drop them on the box. Files are listed with their size and status, and can upload automatically, on a button click or programmatically, with progress, cancel, retry and remove for each file. Files that exceed the limits are listed with the reason.": "",
  "Selecting, dropping and uploading": "",
  "`upload` is your own function for sending a file. Report progress, stop on the signal, and resolve to the response. Alternatively, with `uploadUrl`, the uploader sends the file itself, either in one request or in chunks (`chunkSize`).": "",
  "Upload modes": "",
  "Uploading to a server": "",
  "The uploader posts a form with the file in `uploadField` (`file` by default) to `uploadUrl`, using `uploadHeaders`. A 2xx response becomes the item's `response`, and JSON is parsed. With `chunkSize`, each chunk carries `Content-Range` and the `chunkIndex` and `chunkCount` fields.": "",
  "The button opens the file dialog. Files can also be dropped on the box, which is highlighted while they are over it.": "",
  "A file that does not meet `accept`, the size limits or `maxFiles` is listed as rejected with the reason, and is not added to the value.": "",
  "Uploads start on selection, on the Upload button, or programmatically. Each row shows progress and a Cancel button during the upload, then “Uploaded” or the failure with Retry. The server response is available as the item's `response`, with JSON parsed.": "",
  "With `chunkSize`, the file is sent in chunks, each in a request with `Content-Range: bytes start-end/total`, and progress covers the whole file.": "",
  "Each row has a remove button. A running upload is stopped first.": "",
  "The select button is the field's control. The label is associated with it, and Space and Enter open the dialog.": "",
  "A list of rows with the name, size and status as text, a progress bar named after the file, and buttons named “Cancel the upload of …”, “Retry” and “Remove …”.": "",
  "Rejection reasons and failures use the kit language or the server's message.": "",
  "The field. `data-dragover` while files are over it.": "Field. Dosyalar üzerindeyken `data-dragover`.",
  "The select button, the hint and the Upload button.": "",
  "The list and each row. `data-status` on the row.": "Liste ve her satır. Satırda `data-status`.",
  "Units: the box with files over it, the two buttons (`hover`, `pressed`, `focus`, `disabled`), the hint, the list, a row per status, the file glyph and the text.": "",
  "Places: the field box as a drop zone (a dashed frame, its corners and its padding) and the row buttons.": "",
  "The spacing in the box, in a button and in a row.": "",
  "The accepted files, excluding rejected ones. `x-model` provides two-way binding.": "",
  "Allows several files at once. `false` keeps only the most recent one.": "",
  "The accepted file types, as in `<input type=\"file\">`: `.png,.jpg`, `image/*`, `application/pdf`.": "",
  "Size limits in bytes. A file outside the limits is listed as rejected with the reason.": "",
  "The maximum number of files.": "",
  "Allows files to be dropped on the box.": "",
  "`instant` uploads on selection, `button` adds an Upload button, and `manual` uses `upload()` programmatically. The default is `instant` with `uploadUrl` or `upload`, and `manual` otherwise.": "",
  "Where and how the uploader sends a file itself, using XMLHttpRequest with progress, as a form with the file in `uploadField`.": "",
  "Bytes per request. The file is sent in chunks, each with `Content-Range` and the `chunkIndex` and `chunkCount` fields, and the last response is used.": "",
  "A custom upload function used instead of `uploadUrl`. Call `report(0…1)` to report progress and stop on `signal`. The value it resolves to becomes the response.": "",
  "Kit default": "",
  "The button, the hint next to it and the Upload button.": "",
  "The list of files below the box.": "",
  "Every file in the list with its state: `file`, `status` (`ready`, `uploading`, `done`, `error`, `aborted`, `invalid`), `progress`, `response` and `message`.": "",
  "Indicates that an upload is running.": "",
  "Opens the browser's file dialog, the same as the button.": "",
  "Adds files as if the user selected them. The limits apply, `onFilesAdded` is raised, and uploads start according to the mode.": "",
  "Uploads the waiting files, or one of them. This is what `manual` mode calls.": "",
  "Stops an upload (the file remains, marked as canceled), removes a file, or removes all files.": "",
  "Occurs when files are selected or dropped (`files`, `refused`). Set `cancel = true` to accept none.": "",
  "Reports each stage of a file's upload, with `item` and `file`, and `error` on failure.": "",
  "Occurs when the accepted files change.": ""
}
